Builder Pattern
Used to construct complex objects step by step.

It useful when the object being built has many optional parts (optional attributes) or requires multiple steps for construction.

Without Builder Pattern :
Object construction is complex and tightly coupled with the object’s class,
making it hard to create different representations or configurations.
· As the number of attributes increases, you need multiple constructors to cover all possible combinations.
If you use only one constructor, your constructor is long and you have to remember the order of the properties to pass.

With Builder Pattern :
Object creation is separated from its representation,
allowing flexible and incremental construction of complex objects,
and supporting different configurations and representations.